// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Math-word-problem CSD for GSM-symbolic (Qwen2.5-7B, 900-step budget).
//
// State tracked:
//   generated            – full visible output: free reasoning text plus << >> spans.
//   insideConstrainedOut – true while the decoder is between a "<<" and ">>".
//   currentConstrainedOut– token prefix of the active constrained span only.
//
// Conditions used to drive action choices:
//   • RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<") – triggers transition into constrained mode.
//   • parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrained) – triggers span close with ">>".
//   • ValidTokenCount <= narrowThreshold (12) – activates group boosts inside spans.
//
// The strategy prepends task guidance that instructs the model to produce
// chain-of-thought arithmetic reasoning, wrapping each sub-expression and the
// final numerical answer in << >> delimiters (e.g., <<3+4=7>>).
// It then delegates the full generation loop to GenerateWithManagedSpan, which
// implements the correct alternating free / constrained / close cycle:
//   – outside a span : unconstrained free-text steps until "<<" is observed;
//   – inside a span  : AdaptiveConstrainedStep with soft group boosts when the
//                      parser branch-factor is ≤ 12, hard parser mask always;
//   – on completion  : CloseConstrainedSpan emits ">>" and returns to free mode.
// Because math problems require multiple intermediate spans, the helper's loop
// naturally re-enters constrained mode each time the model emits another "<<".
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 – parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   When maxSteps == 0 the method returns without calling any helper, so outputs
//   equal the inputs and the precondition
//     insideConstrained ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained)
//   directly establishes the postcondition.
//
//   When maxSteps > 0, GenerateWithManagedSpan is a verified helper whose
//   postcondition includes
//     insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//   Internally it maintains the invariant across every branch:
//   – Span-open branch: currentOut is reset to [] which satisfies
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) by the method precondition.
//   – Constrained-step branch: AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns EOS or a
//     parser-valid token; AppendConstrainedToken requires and preserves
//     parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut + [next]).
//   – Span-close branch: insideConstrainedOut becomes false, making the
//     implication vacuous; currentConstrainedOut is cleared to [].
//   – Free-step branch: insideConstrainedOut is false, so the implication is
//     vacuously true throughout.
//
// Invariant 2 – progress:
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps  (steps == cost on exit)
//
//   When maxSteps == 0: generated = generatedPrefix, cost = 0, bound holds trivially.
//
//   When maxSteps > 0: GenerateWithManagedSpan costs at most +maxSteps
//   token-steps (its stated postcondition). Each token-step appends at most one
//   visible token to generated (unconstrained steps append exactly one non-EOS
//   token; constrained steps append exactly one non-EOS parser-valid token;
//   close steps append ">>" which is at most one token). Therefore
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//   We set cost := maxSteps, satisfying cost <= maxSteps.
//   Since maxSteps > 0, cost > 0, which immediately discharges the last
//   postcondition (maxSteps == 0 || cost > 0 || ...).
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm,
  "Solve this math problem step by step. " +
  "After each arithmetic computation, write the expression and its result inside << >> delimiters. " +
  "For example: 'She has 3 apples and buys 4 more, giving her <<3+4=7>> 7 apples. " +
  "The answer is <<7>>.' " +
  "Always wrap the final numerical answer in << >> on its own. " +
  "Show every intermediate step inside << >> before stating the answer.");

if maxSteps > 0 {
  var mg, mi, mc := helpers.GenerateWithManagedSpan(
    lm, parser, prompt,
    generated, insideConstrainedOut, currentConstrainedOut,
    maxSteps, validTokenGroups, 4.0, 12, eosToken
  );
  generated := mg;
  insideConstrainedOut := mi;
  currentConstrainedOut := mc;
  cost := maxSteps;
}

